          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\n**History of Present Illness:**  \nThe patient has generalized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures beginning at 13 years of age. Current seizure frequency is approximately one seizure per week. The epilepsy is classified as drug-responsive with a structural etiology.\n\n**Current Antiseizure Medications:**  \n- Valproate  \n- Lacosamide  \n\n**Seizure Burden:**  \nGeneralized tonic-clonic seizures occurring approximately once weekly.\n\n**Imaging:**  \nBrain MRI demonstrates focal cortical dysplasia, Palmini type IIb.\n\n**Assessment:**  \nGeneralized epilepsy with generalized tonic-clonic seizures, onset at age 13, associated with a structural etiology. Drug-responsive status is noted.\n\n**Plan:**  \nContinue the current antiseizure medication regimen of valproate and lacosamide. Continue tracking seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,  \nEpilepsy Clinic",
